				58,
				6
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Refine documentation and update in Vine gRPC layer\n\nStreamline and update module documentation across DevLog, Error, Host, Library, and Multiplexer to reflect current implementation. Remove outdated synthesis comments and clarify the role of each module. The Multiplexer documentation is updated to reflect that reverse-RPC and cancellation are handled but currently no-op, preserving equivalence with the unary fallback path.\n\nNo functional changes. Impact: improved documentation clarity for Vine consumers.",
			"SHA": "5a51fae9f238cf03e89fa7f7e1918141ea63b50f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T10:18:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				58,
				8
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Update module documentation and constants in Vine server module\n\nThis commit updates the server module documentation to improve clarity and remove outdated synthesis comments. The server-side gRPC scaffolding is updated with refined documentation for the server module. The changes include:\n- Removing outdated synthesis comments and reformatting documentation in the Server module.\n- Clarifying the role of each module in the Vine server module.\n- The impact includes improved documentation for the Vine server module.",
			"SHA": "50e37511b8b812229fede256c92396d37d3535a5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T10:18:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				58,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Vine): Streamline client module documentation and timeouts\n\nRemove outdated synthesis comments and reformat documentation in `Source/Client/` modules to improve clarity. Clarify timeout behavior in `SendRequest` and refine references to default timeout constants. Update module-level documentation to reflect current behavior without verbose historical context.\n\nThis reduces noise in the documentation while preserving all technical accuracy for implementers.",
			"SHA": "d9f4f35f3725d095ca845b5cc9149d92fb780200"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T09:45:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠃⠀⠀",
				58,
				26
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Populate Server module with constants, helpers, and notification atoms\n\nReplace the intentionally-empty `Source/Server/mod.rs` placeholder with the canonical server-side scaffolding extracted from Mountain's in-tree Vine module. Add `Constants` (default ports, timeouts, message-size cap), `ValidateSocketAddress` (pre-flight parsing and privileged-port warning), `SpawnBindTask` (detached `tokio::spawn` with uniform dev-log instrumentation), and `SpawnBindTaskWithShutdown` (graceful-shutdown variant for daemon embedders like Air). Introduce the `Notification` submodule with `RelayToSky` support and nine pure renderer-event relay atoms (`OutputAppend`, `OutputClear`, `OutputCreate`, `OutputDispose`, `OutputShow`, `OutputChannelClear`, `OutputChannelDispose`, `OutputChannelShow`, `ProgressComplete`). Regenerate `Source/Generated/vine.rs` from `Proto/Vine.proto` so the crate compiles with real protobuf types. Apply rustfmt to `Source/Client/mod.rs`, `Source/Error.rs`, `Source/Host.rs`, `Source/Library.rs`, and `Source/Multiplexer.rs` for consistent line-wrapping.\n\nThis continues Phase 2 of the Mountain-Crate-Split plan: the Vine crate now has both a functional client surface (from the initial bootstrap) and a functional server surface, so Mountain and Air can begin consuming it instead of their in-tree modules.",
			"SHA": "ed69779327946fb821fb124b3582135da75d02c8"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1780841375325
}